  "notes": "The lane's hybrid corner, modelled on the later rhythm-pop era because that is the half the research pairs with a backbeat class: \"the rhythm-pop era 100–130 with a **half-time-feeling** backbeat on 3\". `halfTime` is true and the snare is `halftime_3`; the 77–100 straight songwriter era is the other class and is named here rather than encoded. Three drum deltas are quoted from that later era — \"kick on 1 and the '&' of 2\", \"clap/snare on 3\", and \"stuttered 16th/32nd hat fills and vocal-chop percussion\", which is the 16/32 roll vocabulary at 0.6 a bar and the two-lane vocal-chop perc block. The bass is \"sub-heavy synth bass with portamento slides between roots, gapped around the kick\" — a synth bass, so no `bass808` block is authored and the inherited null is what lets a bassline exist at all; the slides are `glideProb` 0.4, the highest in this batch. Harmony is \"modal minor/major mixture; two-chord vamps and i–VII–VI cycles\" with \"parallel-minor borrowings, flattened 6th\" from the early Portuguese-fado and Brazilian colour, so the families are short and phrygian carries weight. The melody is \"rhythmically busy with a wide interval leap into the hook\", i.e. a high density with a real `octaveJumpProb`. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research says so and marks the tempo values **[LOW-CONF]**. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and `bpm.mode` 112.",
